    "scientific_physical_explanation": "Because the Moon is tidally locked in synchronous rotation with Earth, the Earth does not rise or set in the conventional sense from the lunar nearside; instead, it executes a small elliptical libration pattern (~\u00b17.9\u00b0 in longitude, ~\u00b16.7\u00b0 in latitude). At Malapert A (80.13\u00b0 S, 1.44\u00b0 E), the site sits nearly on the Prime Lunar Meridian facing Earth. Throughout the entire 14-day mission window, Earth's elevation remains between +8.83\u00b0 and +16.03\u00b0 above the local horizontal plane. In that direction (azimuth ~353\u00b0 to ~5\u00b0), the local terrain horizon obstruction is relatively low (+2.72\u00b0 to +3.30\u00b0). Consequently, Earth's minimum clearance above the terrain horizon is +5.55\u00b0 (occurring at 2024-03-06T06:00:00Z). Earth therefore remains continuously in geometric line-of-sight throughout the entire 14-day interval. CRITICAL CAVEAT: This proves geometric line-of-sight clearance (Geometric Earth Visibility / DTE Proxy). It does NOT guarantee 100% communications link availability, which depends on DSN ground station scheduling, Earth rotational view periods from Goldstone/Madrid/Canberra, lunar lander antenna orientation, and RF link budget."
  },
